  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The index is applied only to the municipalities within a single province, Gauteng, which may limit its immediate generalizability to rural or less urbanized regions of South Africa.",
      "what": "The study developed a Climate Environmental Vulnerability Index (CEVI) for municipalities in South Africa's Gauteng Province using 17 standardized indicators spanning exposure, sensitivity, and adaptive capacity from 2010 to 2024. Using Principal Component Analysis, the framework measures and maps localized climate vulnerability across geographically proximate urban areas.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that local differences in adaptive capacity and socio-economic conditions, rather than climate exposure itself, are the primary drivers of vulnerability variation, proving that uniform provincial climate policies are insufficient compared to targeted municipal-level interventions."
